{"resourceIdentifier":"1201","resourceName":"Gola REDD project","description":"The Gola REDD project aims to conserve the forested areas of the Gola Rainforest National Park (GRNP). The GRNP and adjacent forests are Sierra Leone’s largest remaining area of Upper Guinea Tropical Forest, a forest type recognised as a global biodiversity hotspot (Myers et al 2000).  The area contains 60 threatened species, including 8 endangered and 1 critically endangered species (Klop et al. 2008).  Conservation actions as a direct result of the Gola REDD project will protect these species, preserve 68,515 ha of tropical forest and conserve 4,394,315 tonnes of CO2-e during the first 10 years of the project, as well as provide livelihood support to the 114 impoverished communities that surround the GRNP.","location":{"latitude":7.606174,"longitude":-11.020161},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2025-04-21","endExclusive":"2025-05-22","endInclusive":"2025-05-21"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1201"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Eastern and Southern Provinces"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Gola Rainforest Conservation LG"},{"type":"string","value":"United Kingdom"},{"type":"string","value":"+44 7956893731"},{"type":"string","value":"richard.dixon@rspb.org.uk"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Verification approval requested"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"1201"},{"type":"bufferSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"1201"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"498667"}]},{"code":"TOTAL_BUFFER_POOL_CREDITS","values":[{"type":"integer","value":633861}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Agriculture Forestry and Other Land Use"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_SUBCATERGOR